---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
	title="Privacy | emin.de"
	description="What this site collects: no analytics, no cookies, no third-party scripts, no tracking pixels. Only standard web server access logs."
	path="/privacy"
	markdownPath="/privacy/index.md"
>
	<h1>Privacy</h1>
	<p class="lede">Short version: there is no tracking on this site, so there is not much to disclose.</p>

	<h2>What is not collected</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>No analytics product, first or third party.</li>
		<li>No cookies are set by this site.</li>
		<li>No advertising or retargeting pixels.</li>
		<li>No third-party fonts, scripts or embeds. Every asset is served from this domain.</li>
		<li>No account system, so no personal data is stored.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>What is collected</h2>
	<p>
		The web server writes standard access logs: IP address, timestamp, requested path, response status, user agent
		and referrer. These exist to operate the server and to count how often AI crawlers and agents fetch content.
		They are not joined to any other dataset and are not sold or shared.
	</p>

	<h2>If you email</h2>
	<p>
		Mail sent to hello@emin.de is stored in a normal mailbox and kept as long as the conversation is useful. It is
		not added to a marketing list, because there is no marketing list.
	</p>

	<h2>Agents and API requests</h2>
	<p>
		Requests to the public API and the MCP server are logged the same way as page requests. The paid corpus endpoint
		processes an x402 payment challenge; payment settlement happens on a public blockchain and is outside this
		site's control. No payment identifiers are stored beyond what the server log records.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>Questions about this page: <a href="mailto:hello@emin.de">hello@emin.de</a>.</p>
</Base>
